  "description": "The master of science degree in geographic information science is designed to be completed in 3 to 5 semesters. The program is suited for students who wish to gain expertise in geographic information systems and science (GIS/GISc) for a wide range of professional applications. The program is a good fit for those who want to begin or advance their career in GIS in the public or private sector. Students may apply to the program having successfully completed a four-year degree at an accredited academic institution. A cumulative grade point average of at least 3.0 in the last two years of undergraduate education is required to be admitted to the program.",
